\startchapter[reference=conclusion, title={Conclusion}]

Single-cell RNA-Seq has grown to be an extensive and active field of science, with new challenges coming up through integration of different kinds of data and the possibilities of ever-growing dataset sizes.
Going up to the hundreds of thousands, they allow to abandon the notion of discrete cell types and to explore the continuous processes at play.
Destiny and the gene relevance method presented in this thesis prove to be a valuable contributions in this direction.
\TODO[can I write that?!]

% extensibility and openness
As demands on reliability at scale grow along demands posed to algorithms, more practices from software engineering are finding their way into biological science.
For example instead of ad-hoc text-based formats, incompatibly modified to suit situational needs, extensible standards are born from collaboration of scientists.
Open source analysis frameworks have been designed to offer an open and welcoming environment for new as well as established analysts and method developers.
My contributions towards more reproducible, scalable and interconnectible scientific programming have helped to bring these changes along.

